From 5ab20335db308c7f0ef3e5fcec0cb4443f59cf6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:27:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add a per-line #delivery: ink tag for voiced lines

Voiced lines now hold only spoken words; how a line is spoken goes in a
#delivery: tag on that line. The note joins the voice style in the TTS
prompt for that line only, is never shown, and enters the cache key only
when present, so every untagged line keeps its existing key and clip.

Person-chat sends the note with the line; the endpoint accepts only a
note the scenario's ink gives that line. The walker, extractor, batch,
sidecars, tts:wasted and the pruner key it the same way. Voiced phone
calls do not send a note yet. dialoguelint warns on inline asterisk
cues in voiced person-chat lines (inline-direction). tts-audio rule 7
and the ink guide describe the new rule.
