diff --git a/docs/achitechture/physical_pentest_followup/VOICE_DELIVERY_TAG_BUILD_LOG.md b/docs/achitechture/physical_pentest_followup/VOICE_DELIVERY_TAG_BUILD_LOG.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..8a99b38ca
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/achitechture/physical_pentest_followup/VOICE_DELIVERY_TAG_BUILD_LOG.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Build log: per-line voice delivery tag (B10, C4)
+
+Branch `build/voice-direction-tag`, 2026-11-10. User decision (C4): voiced lines hold only spoken words; a per-line performance note goes in an ink tag. No scenario ink was changed and no audio was generated.
+
+## What was built
+
+- **Tag:** `#delivery: quietly, almost to herself`, at the end of the line or on the line above. Named `delivery` rather than `direction` (which in this game already means a door side or a facing) or the plan's `perform:`; it is the voice term for how a line is said. The last non-empty `delivery:` tag on a line wins; whitespace is collapsed.
+- **Prompt:** `TtsService.speech_style` appends "For this line only: <note>." to the voice style in the `speech_metadata` annotation. The spoken text is unchanged and the note is never shown.
+- **Key:** `cache_key_for_normalized` adds `|delivery:<normalised note>` only when there is a note, so every untagged key is byte-for-byte what it was. Checked three ways: a literal committed m01 key, a sweep of every committed current-model sidecar, and the extractor's keys for every scenario before and after the change (8,475 keys, identical).
+- **Client:** `systems/tts-delivery.js` reads the tag; person-chat sends it as `delivery` with the line (`TTSManager.play/preload`, `ApiClient.getTTS`, which adds the field only when there is a note). `chat-helpers.js` never runs it as a game action.
+- **Server:** the endpoint accepts a note only when the scenario's ink gives that line that note for that speaker (`TtsLineExtractor#delivered_by?`, else 403; over 200 characters, 400). A tagged line has its own clip; on a keyless server with no tagged clip it plays the untagged clip or the previous-model clip rather than nothing.
+- **Agreement:** `InkLineWalker` keeps a line's tags (and now carries only a `delivery:` tag over an empty line, as `InkEngine#continue` does); `TtsLineExtractor` entries carry `delivery`; the batch, sidecars (`delivery` field, only when present), `tts:wasted` and the pruner's expected set all key it the same way.
+- **Phone calls:** voiced phone calls do not send a note yet; the extractor gives their lines none, so client and batch agree. Supporting them needs the note carried from `phoneStepLines` to `_speakCallLine`, including the preloaded opening.
+- **Lint:** `dialoguelint.mjs` rule `inline-direction` (warn): an asterisk cue in a voiced person-chat line. Skips choices, the player's lines, narration, phone inks and emphasis between two words (`I *never* said`). 401 hits across `scenarios/` today (m01: 17).
+- **Docs:** `tts-audio` rule 7 rewritten; `README_ink_best_practices.md` section "Voiced lines hold only spoken words"; the two review skills that called inline emotes fine now point to the tag. `docs/agents/PASS4_BRIEF.md` line 30 still describes inline cues and is left for the orchestrator.
+
+## Tests
+
+`test/unit/break_escape/tts_delivery_test.rb` (14), seven new cases in `test/controllers/break_escape/tts_controller_test.rb`, `test/js/tts-delivery.test.mjs`, one new case in `test/js/dialoguelint.test.mjs`; `finale-voiced-calls.test.mjs` updated for the new `getTTS` call.
